# =============================================================================
# ETBZ service - example environment
# =============================================================================
# This file contains PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. It must never contain a real
# credential, token, key or endpoint. Copy it to `.env` for local use; `.env`
# is git-ignored and is never read by the service itself.
#
# The ETBZ configuration loader is a pure function over an explicitly supplied
# environment record (see src/app/configuration/config.ts). It does NOT read
# any file, and in particular it never reads /root/.env or any other host
# configuration. Loading this file into the process environment is the job of
# the operator or the container runtime, not of the service.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED in ETBZ-9 - readiness-relevant
# A missing or malformed value here makes GET /ready answer 503 (fail closed).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deployment environment. REQUIRED, no default of any kind, and in particular
# no implicit "production".
# Allowed: local | development | test | staging | production
ETBZ_ENV=local

# Log level. REQUIRED.
# Allowed: debug | info | warn | error
LOG_LEVEL=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL in ETBZ-9 - readiness-relevant when present
# May be omitted; a malformed value still fails readiness.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# HTTP listen port. Defaults to 8120 when unset.
ETBZ_PORT=8120

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD / PROVENANCE - injected by the image build, not by an operator
# Not readiness-relevant. Verified by the provenance gate, not by /ready.
# A missing or placeholder revision fails the image build, never defaults to
# "unknown".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ETBZ_GIT_COMMIT=<40-character git commit sha - set by docker build --build-arg>
# ETBZ_BUILD_VERSION=<build version identifier - set by docker build --build-arg>
# ETBZ_SOURCE_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/DYAI2025/ETBZ
# ETBZ_BUILD_TIMESTAMP=<RFC3339 build timestamp - set by docker build --build-arg>

# =============================================================================
# RESERVED FOR LATER SLICES - NOT READ BY ETBZ-9
# =============================================================================
# The names below are documented so that operators can see where the
# configuration surface is heading. They are NOT part of the ETBZ-9
# configuration schema: setting them has no effect, they cannot change
# EtbzConfig, and they can neither satisfy nor fail readiness in this slice.
# Each becomes real only in the slice that implements the capability behind it,
# together with its own readiness capability.
#
# Secrets are never committed here - the placeholders are intentionally empty.
#
#   FuFirE integration (out of scope in ETBZ-9):
#     ETBZ_FUFIRE_BASE_URL=
#     ETBZ_FUFIRE_API_KEY=
#
#   Etsy / marketplace intake (out of scope in ETBZ-9):
#     ETBZ_ETSY_SHOP_ID=
#     ETBZ_ETSY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
#   Persistence (out of scope in ETBZ-9):
#     ETBZ_DATABASE_URL=
#
#   Rendering / delivery (out of scope in ETBZ-9):
#     ETBZ_RENDER_ENGINE=
#     ETBZ_DELIVERY_MODE=
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# ETBZ-25B - NARRATIVE LLM PROVIDER ROUTES
# =============================================================================
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never commit a real credential here.
#
# These are read by `src/app/configuration/llm-routes.ts`, which - like every
# other ETBZ loader - is a PURE function over an explicitly supplied environment
# record. It reads no file and never touches `process.env` itself.
#
# WHICH routes are approved, and in which order, is product truth and lives in
# `APPROVED_LLM_ROUTES` in that module. Only the base URL, the model id and the
# credential are configuration.
#
# NO-CHARGE RULE (fail-closed): a route is ELIGIBLE only when its configured
# model id carries the provider's explicit zero-price marker - it must END with
# `-free` or `:free`. A model without that marker may be billable, so the route
# is skipped rather than tried. ETBZ cannot verify what a provider does not
# publish, and the approved development cost cap is 0.00 EUR.
#
# Route 1 - TokenRouter
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_TOKENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://api.example-provider.invalid/v1
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_TOKENROUTER_MODEL=vendor/model-free
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_TOKENROUTER_API_KEY=
#
# Route 2 - Gemini (OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
# NOTE: this endpoint carries no per-model price marker. Whether a call is
# billed depends on the billing state of the key's project, which the API does
# not report back, so under a 0.00 EUR cap this route stays INELIGIBLE.
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.example.invalid/v1beta/openai/
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_GEMINI_MODEL=
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
#
# Route 3 - OpenCode (OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENCODE_BASE_URL=https://opencode.example.invalid/v1
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENCODE_PRIMARY_MODEL=model-free
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENCODE_API_KEY=
#
# Route 4 - OpenRouter
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.example.invalid/api/v1
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENROUTER_MODEL=vendor/model:free
ETBZ_EXAMPLE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#
# COST CAP. Both are optional; the values below are the ONLY accepted ones.
# There is no variable that authorises a billable call: `assertNoPaidPathAuthorized`
# refuses one unconditionally, because a human approval an operator can grant
# themselves by exporting a variable is not an approval. Raising the cap is a
# reviewed code change in a later slice.
LLM_ALLOW_PAID=false
LLM_PAID_COST_CAP_USD=0
#
# Bound into the live-run evidence record so a reading can be traced to the
# exact commit that produced it. Set by the operator running `npm run golden-reading`.
# ETBZ_CANDIDATE_SHA=<40-character git commit sha>
